<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:h="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" version="1.0" name="Packet" initial="collecting"><metadata><h:section id="documentation"><h:h2>Packet — actor contract</h:h2><h:p><h:strong>Actor invariant: </h:strong>An export is a digest-verified snapshot of individually kept revisions plus unresolved annotations. No separate approval state or signature exists.</h:p><h:p><h:strong>Specification: </h:strong>ACT-PACKET in <h:a href="../system.xml">system.xml</h:a>. These comments use XHTML namespace h: and are not executable SCXML actions.</h:p><h:h3>I/O contracts invoked by this actor</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-PACKET-COMPILE">review.packet.compile</h:a> — CompileRequest → CompileResult | Fault; local-write, safe-idempotent, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-018, FL-021; requirements: REQ-043, REQ-044, REQ-045, REQ-047, REQ-068</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-PACKET-EXPORT">review.packet.export</h:a> — PacketExportRequest → PacketExportResult | Fault; local-write, never, 12000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-021, FL-046; requirements: REQ-048, REQ-096</h:li></h:ul></h:section></metadata><state id="collecting">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-collecting"><h:h3>State: collecting</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>packet.compile</h:code> → compiling</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="packet.compile" target="compiling"/>
  </state>
  <state id="compiling">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-compiling"><h:h3>State: compiling</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>packet.ready</h:code> → ready<h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-PACKET-COMPILE"> [typed result: IO-PACKET-COMPILE]</h:a></h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="packet.ready" target="ready"/>
  </state>
  <state id="ready">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-ready"><h:h3>State: ready</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>packet.export</h:code> → exported</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="packet.export" target="exported"/>
  </state>
  <state id="exported">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-exported"><h:h3>State: exported</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>packet.stale</h:code> → stale</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="packet.stale" target="stale"/>
  </state>
  <state id="stale">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-stale"><h:h3>State: stale</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>packet.compile</h:code> → compiling</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="packet.compile" target="compiling"/>
  </state>
</scxml>
